Sure thing.  In System Preferences > Accounts > Login Options you will
need:

"Automatically log in as:" DEselected;
"Display login window as: Name and password" checked.

Now, reboot the system.  You will be prompted for login credentials.
Enter ">console" for the username and press enter (password left
blank).  You will be dropped into a fullscreen shell that will then
prompt again for your login info.  Here you will use one of the actual
accounts on your system.  If you want color, append to your
~/.bash_profile the line "export TERM=xterm-color".

